/-
# `ConRon.Refine2.Frontend.PreludeText` — the 67 prelude chunks are the twin's

**Task #97-P5-Front round 2.**  `frontend/prelude_text.rs` (generated by
`scripts/gen-prelude.sh`) and `Arena/Frontend/PreludeText.lean` (generated by
`scripts/gen-prelude-lean.sh`) split the same 16 922 bytes into the same 67
chunks of at most 256.  One lemma per chunk says the two chunks are the same
bytes — each is closed by `decide` on a literal list, by the kernel, with no
`native_decide` — and `builtin_prelude_text_refines` folds the port's 67
`push_chunk`s (`Vec::extend_from_slice`, `extend_u8_val`) against the twin's
67 `pushChunk`s (`ByteArray.append`).

This is the ONE fact about the two generators a proof needs and that no proof
can get from either generator: their `--check` gates each compare against
con-leche's ndjson, not against each other.

## `sorry` count in this file: 0
-/
